      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/anoka_nebraska",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "By 1905, Anoka boasted about 30 businesses, including grain elevators, a hotel, and a weekly newspaper.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/anoka_nebraska",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Today, Anoka remains a quiet agricultural community in Boyd County, preserving its pioneer heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/anoka_nebraska",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Anoka sits near a creek, its name possibly derived from a Dakota Sioux term meaning 'on both sides' of the creek.",
